My friend Eliza has used some online dating sites to find different people to date. She realized that despite the site’s recommendations, she didn’t like everyone she was matched with. After some soul-searching, she realized that there were three types of people she was dating:

People she didn’t like
The people she loved in small doses
The people she loved in large doses
After finding out about this, Eliza couldn’t figure out what made a person fall into one of these categories. They were all recommended to her by the dating site. The people she liked in small doses were good to see Monday through Friday, but on weekends she preferred spending time with the people she liked in large doses. Eliza asked us to help him filter future matches to categorize them. Also, Eliza has collected data that is not recorded by the dating site, but she finds it useful in selecting who to date.
